repeats of erythrocyte ankyrin form two distinct but cooperative binding sites for the erythrocyte anion exchanger</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem</source><volume>270</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>22050</fpage><lpage>22057</lpage>a<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7665627</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="MichaelyandBennett1995b"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Michaely</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bennett</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanism for binding site diversity on ankyrin. Comparison of binding sites on ankyrin for neurofascin and the Cl<sup>&#x02212;</sup>/HCO3<sup>&#x02212;</sup> anion exchanger</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem</source><volume>270</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>31298</fpage><lpage>31302</lpage>b<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8537399</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Nassaretal1987"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nassar</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Reedy</surname><given-names>M.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>P.A.W.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Developmental changes in the ultrastructure and sarcomere shortening in the isolated rabbit ventricular myocyte</article-title><source>Circ. Res.</source><volume>61</volume><year>1987</year><fpage>465</fpage><lpage>483</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2441892</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="NelsonandVeshnock1987"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>W.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Veshnock</surname><given-names>P.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ankyrin binding to (Na<sup>++</sup> K<sup>+</sup>)ATPase and implications for the organization of membrane domains in polarized cells</article-title><source>Nature.</